<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net40;net45;netstandard2.0;netstandard2.1</TargetFrameworks>

    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>$(Generate_ImmediateReflection)</GeneratePackageOnBuild>

    <Title>ImmediateReflection</Title>
    <RootNamespace>ImmediateReflection</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>ImmediateReflection</AssemblyName>

    <!-- Overridden by CI -->
    <Version>1.0.0</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>1.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>1.0.0</FileVersion>

    <Copyright>Copyright © 2019-2026</Copyright>
    <Description>.NET library that aims to provide a faster usage of C# reflection features.
Especially the usage of constructors, members accessors (get/set) and attributes.

It provides these features while trying to keep an API as similar as the standard Reflection API.

Supported platforms:
- .NET Standard 2.0+
- .NET Core 2.0+
- .NET Framework 4.0+

Supports Source Link

See benchmarks here: https://kernelith.github.io/ImmediateReflection/documentation/benchmarks.html.</Description>

    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>ImmediateReflection</PackageId>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>➟ Release 3.0.0
Updates:
- Big cold start improvement: getters/setters of ImmediateProperty and ImmediateField are now generated on first use, as are the constructors and attributes of ImmediateType and members (creating an ImmediateProperty/ImmediateField is now ~100x faster and allocates far less).
- Accesses to the internal caches through the public API (TypeAccessor, ImmediateType, attributes, ...) no longer allocate on a cache hit and are ~2x faster.
- TypeAccessor.Get&lt;T&gt;() has a dedicated fast path when the type is known at compile time.
- Faster access to the attributes of types and members (fewer allocations on GetAttribute(s)/GetAllAttributes).
- Copy of value types, string and Type is faster and no longer boxes needlessly.
- Getters returning a boolean no longer allocate (boxed true/false values are cached).
- Generated dynamic methods are now bound to a closed delegate, which makes calling the generated getters/setters faster.
- Improve Equals and hash code computation of ImmediateFields and ImmediateProperties.

Misc:
- Library code migrated to C# 10 (file scoped namespaces, nullable enabled, polyfills for old targets).</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageTags>C# Reflection Fast Immediate Performance Delegate Dynamic</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Targets defines -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='net40'">
    <AssemblyTitle>ImmediateReflection .NET 4.0</AssemblyTitle>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='net45'">
    <AssemblyTitle>ImmediateReflection .NET 4.5</AssemblyTitle>
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);SUPPORTS_AGGRESSIVE_INLINING</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='netstandard2.0'">
    <AssemblyTitle>ImmediateReflection .NET Standard 2.0</AssemblyTitle>
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);SUPPORTS_AGGRESSIVE_INLINING</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='netstandard2.1'">
    <AssemblyTitle>ImmediateReflection .NET Standard 2.1</AssemblyTitle>
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);SUPPORTS_AGGRESSIVE_INLINING</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Dependencies -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)'=='netstandard2.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Bcl.HashCode" Version="6.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Reflection.Emit.LightWeight" Version="4.7.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>